# Template. Copy to secrets.sops.env, fill in, encrypt:
#
#   cp secrets.sops.env.example secrets.sops.env
#   $EDITOR secrets.sops.env
#   sops -e -i secrets.sops.env
#
# Two kinds of line, neither of them a value: identifying values, and `pass://` references that
# `pass-cli run` resolves once `sops exec-env` has loaded this file into the environment. No
# braces — `run` resolves bare URIs and ignores braced ones, the inverse of `inject`. See
# .just/tofu.just and docs/src/tofu/index.md.

# The policy PAT, and deliberately not the enrollment PAT ansible/roles/netbird uses
# (config/secrets.sops.yaml). Issued to a Network Admin service user, which covers the groups,
# policies, route and DNS zone this module owns. A PAT inherits its user's role, so that is the
# whole of this token's authority — it cannot mint a setup key.
#
# Account settings (settings.tf) are the exception: Network Admin reads them and cannot write
# them, so the first apply and any later edit to settings.tf need the service user promoted to
# Admin for the duration, then demoted again. The procedure is in
# docs/src/tofu/netbird.md#applying-account-settings.
#
# PATs expire, 365 days out at most. Rotation is
# docs/src/operations/rotation.md#the-netbird-tokens.
NB_PAT=pass://futharkd/netbird-policy/token
